accepted: this would change
size checked against the default server limits; the apply checks each server's own
receivers foo.c.core mail: added foo.c.core, foo.c.lead, foo.d.build; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.core prompt: added foo.d.build; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.core status: added foo.c.core, foo.c.lead, foo.d.build; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.core heartbeat: added foo.c.core, foo.c.lead, foo.d.build; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.lead mail: added foo.c.lead; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.lead status: added foo.c.lead; removed (none)
receivers foo.c.lead heartbeat: added foo.c.lead; removed (none)
template foo.c: added
tags foo.c.core: (none) -> allow:d.build, deny:_none
tags foo.c.lead: (none) -> deny:c.core
rotate and revoke: (none)
new credential (not issued by the apply; the sender's endpoint needs a credential with its new tags): (none)
revoke: (none)
first credential (not issued by the apply; an existing endpoint needs a credential with its tags): foo.c.core, foo.c.lead
inbox not checked: the apply's inbox and narrowing checks were not run, so it may still refuse
